   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	No of legal and policy documents improved
2.	No of climate risk data digitalized
3.	No of multihazard comprehensive risk and vulnerability assessments produced
4.	No of civil servants from Line Ministries sensitized and No. of gender sensitive methodologies developed; No of trainings organized in local level to build and strengthen capacities for planning, budgeting, and mainstreaming CCA
5.	No of workshops organized and No of financing strategies/ mechanisms for scaling up adaptation in the mid- to long-term
6.	No of sectorial adaptation plans developed
7.	No of legal acts, guidelines developed to establish M&amp;E system to CCA
8.	No. of awareness raising workshops conducted</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	NAP identified as priority goal in NAP Framework document of 2019; Weak IMWGCC and IGEO mandate for CCA.
2.	information gaps; data is fragmented, incomplete, and is not readily accessible; limited digitization of climate risk data 
3.	Studies on vulnerability assessments and associated data collection processes remain fragmentary, limited and uncoordinated at the national level; 
4.	climate adaptation planning capacity weaknesses;
5.	limited domestic resources to finance adaptation actions and associated budget priorities, and financing appropriations for funding CCA are absent. 
6.	climate change is not integrated into existing environmental and development policies; 
7.	climate related monitoring and evaluation (M&amp;E), for both adaptation and mitigation, is embryonic. 
8.	a lack of awareness of CCA &#x2013; both at the national and subnational levels;</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
